00:36:20,769 --> 00:36:26,769
Inside Llewyn Davis () is a 2013 period black comedy drama film written,
directed, produced, and edited by Joel and Ethan Coen.

10
00:40:23,076 --> 00:40:29,076
Set in 1961, the film follows one week in the life of Llewyn Davis, played by Oscar Isaac in his breakthrough
role, a folk singer struggling to achieve musical success while keeping his life in order.

11
00:44:25,384 --> 00:44:31,384
The supporting cast includes Carey Mulligan, John Goodman, Garrett Hedlund, F.

12
00:48:27,692 --> 00:48:33,692
Murray Abraham, Justin Timberlake and Adam Driver.

13
00:52:30,000 --> 00:52:36,000
Though Davis is a fictional character, the story was partly
inspired by folk singer Dave Van Ronk's autobiography.

14
00:56:32,307 --> 00:56:38,307
Most of the folk songs performed in the film are sung in full and recorded live.

15
01:00:34,615 --> 01:00:40,615
T Bone Burnett was the executive music producer.

16
01:04:36,923 --> 01:04:42,923
Principal photography took place in early 2012, primarily in New York City.

17
01:08:39,230 --> 01:08:45,230
The film, an international co-production between companies in France, the United Kingdom and the
United States, was financed by StudioCanal before it received an American distributor.

18
01:12:41,538 --> 01:12:47,538
Inside Llewyn Davis premiered at the 2013 Cannes Film Festival
on May 19, 2013, where it won the Grand Prix.

19
01:16:43,846 --> 01:16:49,846
The film was theatrically released in France on November 6, 2013, and in
the United Kingdom on January 24, 2014, by StudioCanal.

20
01:20:46,153 --> 01:20:52,153
It was given a limited release by CBS Films in the United States on December
6, 2013, before opening in a wide release on January 10, 2014.

21
01:24:48,461 --> 01:24:54,461
The film received critical acclaim and was nominated for two Academy Awards (Best Cinematography and Best Sound Mixing) and three Golden Globe
Awards for Best Motion Picture – Comedy or Musical, Best Actor – Motion Picture Musical or Comedy (Isaac), and Best Original Song.

22
01:28:50,769 --> 01:28:56,769
Inside Llewyn Davis has been held in high critical esteem since its release as one of the greatest films ever made, being
voted the 11th-best film of the 21st century in both a 2016 BBC poll and a 2017 The New York Times list.

23
01:32:53,076 --> 01:32:59,076
The film was ranked 14 on Rolling Stone magazine's list of "50 Best Movies of the 2010s" and 2 on
The Hollywood Reporter's list of the "50 Best Films of the 21st Century (So Far)."

24
01:36:55,384 --> 01:37:01,384
The film explores themes of depression, new york city, guitar, winter, cat.

25
01:40:57,692 --> 01:41:03,692
The tone is dark and emotional.
